  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer (config_006, acc 0.653) is the clear best so far, and image-only resnet50 is very weak (config_010, acc 0.208). The critical open question is whether adding image information via fusion provides any complementary signal beyond the strong RNA baseline, or whether the image modality is simply uninformative for this task. This experiment (config_032: multimodal, scvi_n200, resnet50, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, concat fusion) directly tests that question by adding the image branch to the exact best RNA configuration while keeping all other settings identical. Using concat (simplest fusion) and resnet50 (already characterized) limits confounding variables. If performance stays near 0.653, image adds no value and we can deprioritize multimodal configs; if it improves, we know the image carries complementary signal and should then explore ViT and weighted fusion. Under a tight budget, this single experiment most efficiently resolves whether the entire multimodal branch of the search space is worth further investment."
}

